1
00:00:00,540 --> 00:00:02,120
This is for Stuart McFarlane.

2
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:09,980
As I walk these streets alone

3
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:12,380
Through this borough I call home

4
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:14,880
Upon the barren fields of Highbury

5
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:16,460
'Neath the stadiums of stone

6
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:18,720
Through the turnstiles at The Angel

7
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:20,740
See the homeless on the green

8
00:00:20,740 --> 00:00:22,860
From The Cally to The Cross

9
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:24,920
And every shithole in between

10
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:27,840
Pass the church, the mosque, a crack den

11
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:29,360
And the offie on the corner

12
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:31,780
See the brasses from the brothel

13
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:33,640
That pretends to be a sauna

14
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:36,000
Watch the bedlam in the bookies

15
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,200
See the winners and the losers

16
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:40,100
Seeking solace from their sorrow

17
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:42,600
In the local battle cruisers

18
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:44,740
Through the madness in the market

19
00:00:44,740 --> 00:00:46,960
Weathered faces turn to greet ya

20
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:48,640
"Hello guv'nor, how's your mother?"

21
00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:49,920
"You alright, son? Be lucky, geezer"

22
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:52,880
Double pie and mash and liquor

23
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:55,020
A cuppa Rosie Lee, old chap

24
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:57,440
Or watch retired gangsters bicker

25
00:00:57,440 --> 00:00:59,400
Every day in Arthur's café

26
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:01,680
The little fuckers causing trouble

27
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:03,620
For the cozzers make you smile

28
00:01:03,620 --> 00:01:05,880
You meet your muckers for a couple

29
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:08,040
Forget your troubles for a while

30
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:10,100
From The Thornhill to The Hemmy

31
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:12,360
All the faces are the same

32
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:14,580
'Cause the manor might be changing

33
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:17,500
But the people still remain

34
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:23,460
North London forever!

35
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:23,860
Whatever the weather,

36
00:01:25,940 --> 00:01:28,400
these streets are our own

37
00:01:30,460 --> 00:01:33,380
And my heart will leave you never

38
00:01:35,260 --> 00:01:37,600
My blood will forever

39
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:41,680
Run through the stone

40
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:04,740
As I walk these streets alone

41
00:02:04,740 --> 00:02:06,980
Through a kingdom made of chrome

42
00:02:06,980 --> 00:02:09,220
I see them ripping up the cobbles

43
00:02:09,220 --> 00:02:11,320
And tearing down our childhood homes

44
00:02:11,320 --> 00:02:13,360
I see the architecture changing

45
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:15,300
Watch the history disappear

46
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:18,220
And the skyline rearranging

47
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:19,800
Into towers of veneer

48
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:22,000
But I see the remnants of a London

49
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,080
That they thought they could erase

50
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:26,800
Every time I hear the old school

51
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:28,700
Talk about the good old days

52
00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:30,600
Or every time I watch the football

53
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:32,840
And have a ruby with the lads

54
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:35,460
See a hoister selling clobber

55
00:02:35,460 --> 00:02:37,320
Or a dealer shooting bags

56
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:39,840
It's in the single mothers juggling

57
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:41,620
A baby and a job

58
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:44,100
In every single brother struggling

59
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:46,060
That wound up in the dock

60
00:02:46,060 --> 00:02:48,020
It's in the roots and the foundations

61
00:02:48,020 --> 00:02:49,780
Still clinging to the land

62
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:52,700
It's in the bricks that built the Morland

63
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:54,580
And Popham that still stand

64
00:02:54,580 --> 00:02:56,680
It's in my family and my friends

65
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:58,780
In every gram and every Benz

66
00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:00,860
It's in the roots that we inherit

67
00:03:00,860 --> 00:03:03,180
When a generation ends

68
00:03:03,180 --> 00:03:05,300
It's in the ruins of your youth

69
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:07,740
And the faces of your past

70
00:03:07,740 --> 00:03:09,840
'Cause the manor might be changing

71
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:12,660
But the people always last

72
00:03:13,380 --> 00:03:13,940
North London forever!

73
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:16,400
Whatever the weather,

74
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:18,440
these streets are our own

75
00:03:18,440 --> 00:03:18,840
And my heart

76
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:23,960
will leave you never

77
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:29,080
My blood will forever

78
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:32,340
Run through the stone